  "title": "Ibn al-Shatir",
  "summary": "Ibn al-Shatir was born in Damascus around 1305 and became head muwaqqit at the Umayyad Mosque, regulating the times of prayer. He built a large horizontal marble sundial for the mosque's northern minaret; the instrument there now is a late 19th-century copy. He died in Damascus around 1375.",
